<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Power profile for the Ulefone Armor 29 Pro (GQ5012BF1, MT6878).
  Every value below was measured on this phone (2026-11-15/16) from the
  sh366003 fuel gauge; nothing is copied from the vendor placeholder.
  Units: mA, single-cell equivalent (~3.85 V) = the units Android uses for
  capacity on this phone. Method: battery current with the charger power path
  off (USB connected), 24-200 samples per point, medians; CPU pinned to known
  frequencies and its share (from /proc/stat x measured core power) subtracted
  where hardware was exercised. Raw logs: build/btf-kernel/power-measurements.

  cpu.*        per-core power per frequency (1 vs 2 busy cores, fitted a*f+b*f^3);
               idle = awake idle minus suspend floor; suspend = overnight drain
  screen.on    37: screen on at minimum brightness vs off
  screen.full  65: OLED, min->max cost depends on content: +14 on the dark lock
               screen, +127 with colour inversion (~150-300 for full white).
               65 = mixed content (average linear brightness ~0.3).
  gps.on       21.5: tracking with fix, 3 cycles
  wifi         idle 2, scan 25, download +91; controller rx/tx 215 scaled to the
               chip's own reported airtime during that download
  modem        fitted to 5 rate-limited transfers using the modem's own
               ModemActivityInfo counters (excess over idle rates); fit within
               2 %: rx 32, tx L2-3 124, tx L4 148, idle 8 (tail test ~10).
               sleep 0: idle-with-service costs only 2-4 above airplane mode,
               already covered by the idle-time counters. TX levels 0-1 never
               occur here (32 s since boot); given the L2-3 value (upper bound).
  radio.scanning  27.6: manual network scan vs idle
  audio        13.8: speaker, media volume 8/15, -12 dBFS tone (path only 8.4,
               volume 15: 141)
  video        11.7: 1080p H.264 hardware decode at real time
  camera.avg   200: rear camera 1080p preview (front camera: 54)
  camera.flashlight  87.7: torch
  bluetooth    on, LE scan and LE advertising all within 0-3 of off (below the
               gauge's noise): controller idle 1. RX/TX with a connected device
               not measured (no device available) - left out rather than guessed.
  NOT PRESENT: ambient display (always-on display does not activate on this
  build, verified), radio.active (call power - needs a real phone call).
-->
